# Utils

<Admonition type="warning">

These helpers are part of the core's unstable API. They are exported because the components and custom croppers need them, but they may change in any new version of the core.

</Admonition>

All of these are re-exported from `svelte-advanced-cropper`, except [`getMimeType`](#getmimetype).

```ts
import { approximateSize, getCoefficient, loadImage } from 'svelte-advanced-cropper';
```

## Fitting state parts

### fitCoordinates

```ts
function fitCoordinates(state: CropperState, settings: CoreSettings): CropperState;
```

Moves and shrinks the crop until it satisfies the size, aspect ratio and position restrictions and lies inside the visible area.

### fitVisibleArea

```ts
function fitVisibleArea(state: CropperState, settings: CoreSettings): CropperState;
```

Gives the visible area the boundary's aspect ratio, then fits it to the area size and area position restrictions.

### getRoundedCoordinates

```ts
function getRoundedCoordinates(state: CropperState, settings: CoreSettings): Coordinates | null;
```

Rounds the crop to whole pixels while keeping it inside the restrictions. `cropper.getCoordinates()` returns this by default.

## Algorithms

The geometry behind the modifiers, working on plain coordinates rather than on a state.

### moveCoordinatesAlgorithm

```ts
function moveCoordinatesAlgorithm(
	coordinates: Coordinates,
	directions: MoveDirections,
	positionRestrictions: PositionRestrictions
): Coordinates;
```

Moves the coordinates, then pushes them back inside the position restrictions.

### resizeCoordinatesAlgorithm

```ts
function resizeCoordinatesAlgorithm(
	coordinates: Coordinates,
	directions: ResizeDirections,
	options: {
		compensate?: boolean;
		preserveAspectRatio?: boolean;
		allowedDirections?: { left?: boolean; right?: boolean; top?: boolean; bottom?: boolean };
		respectDirection?: 'width' | 'height';
	},
	limitations: ResizeLimitations
): Coordinates;

interface ResizeDirections {
	left: number;
	right: number;
	top: number;
	bottom: number;
}

interface ResizeLimitations {
	aspectRatio: AspectRatio;
	sizeRestrictions: SizeRestrictions;
	positionRestrictions: PositionRestrictions;
}
```

Moves each side of the coordinates outward by the matching amount in `directions` (negative values move it inward) while respecting the limitations.

### anchoredResizeCoordinatesAlgorithm

```ts
function anchoredResizeCoordinatesAlgorithm(
	coordinates: Coordinates,
	anchor: ResizeAnchor,
	directions: MoveDirections,
	options: ResizeOptions,
	limitations: ResizeLimitations
): Coordinates;
```

The handle-based version: converts the drag of the `anchor` handle into side directions, calls `resizeCoordinatesAlgorithm`, and keeps the opposite handle where it was in `options.reference`. Try it on the [Resize Algorithm](/docs/algorithms/resize-algorithm) page.

## Gestures

### touchesToImageTransform

```ts
function touchesToImageTransform(
	touches: SimpleTouch[],
	previousTouches: SimpleTouch[],
	container: HTMLElement,
	options?: { rotate?: boolean; move?: boolean; scale?: boolean }
): ImageTransform;

interface SimpleTouch {
	clientX: number;
	clientY: number;
}
```

Compares two sets of touches and returns the move, scale and rotation between them, relative to `container`. One finger only moves. Several fingers also scale, and exactly two can rotate. Only the kinds enabled in `options` are returned.

### wheelEventToImageTransform

```ts
function wheelEventToImageTransform(
	event: WheelEvent,
	container: HTMLElement,
	ratio?: number
): ImageTransform;
```

Turns a wheel event into a scale around the pointer. `ratio` (default `0.1`) is the zoom step per wheel tick.

## Canvas

### drawCroppedArea

```ts
function drawCroppedArea(
	state: CropperState,
	image: HTMLImageElement | HTMLCanvasElement,
	resultCanvas: HTMLCanvasElement,
	spareCanvas: HTMLCanvasElement,
	options: DrawOptions
): HTMLCanvasElement | null;

interface DrawOptions {
	width?: number;
	height?: number;
	minWidth?: number;
	maxWidth?: number;
	minHeight?: number;
	maxHeight?: number;
	maxArea?: number;
	imageSmoothingQuality?: 'low' | 'medium' | 'high';
	imageSmoothingEnabled?: boolean;
	fillColor?: string;
}
```

Draws the crop into `resultCanvas`. `spareCanvas` is used to pre-render the rotated or flipped image. The output keeps the crop's aspect ratio: `width` and `height` set an exact size, the `min*`/`max*` options bound it, and `maxArea` caps the pixel count. `cropper.getCanvas(options)` calls this with the same options.

## Normalization

The cropper's gestures arrive in screen pixels, while the state is in image pixels. These convert one to the other by multiplying by the [coefficient](#getcoefficient).

### normalizeMoveDirections

```ts
function normalizeMoveDirections(
	state: CropperState,
	directions: Partial<MoveDirections>
): MoveDirections;
```

### normalizeResizeDirections

```ts
function normalizeResizeDirections(
	state: CropperState,
	directions: Partial<ResizeDirections>
): ResizeDirections;
```

### normalizeImageTransform

```ts
function normalizeImageTransform(state: CropperState, transform: ImageTransform): ImageTransform;
```

Converts the move and the scale and rotation centres of an image transform. Note that it changes the object you pass in.

### normalizeCenter

```ts
function normalizeCenter(state: CropperState, center: Point): Point;
```

Converts a point in the boundary to a point in the image.

### normalizeFlip

```ts
function normalizeFlip(state: CropperState, flip: Flip): Flip;
```

Swaps a horizontal and a vertical flip when the image is rotated by about 90°, so that "horizontal" always means horizontal on screen.

## Getters

The settings fields can be values or functions. These resolve them for a given state.

### getSizeRestrictions

```ts
function getSizeRestrictions(state: CropperState, settings: CoreSettings): SizeRestrictions;
```

Missing values are filled with `0` and `Infinity`, and the maximums are capped by the position restrictions.

### getPositionRestrictions

```ts
function getPositionRestrictions(state: CropperState, settings: CoreSettings): PositionRestrictions;
```

### getAreaSizeRestrictions

```ts
function getAreaSizeRestrictions(state: CropperState, settings: CoreSettings): AreaSizeRestrictions;
```

### getAreaPositionRestrictions

```ts
function getAreaPositionRestrictions(
	state: CropperState,
	settings: CoreSettings
): AreaPositionRestrictions;
```

### getAspectRatio

```ts
function getAspectRatio(state: CropperState, settings: CoreSettings): AspectRatio;
```

Always returns `{ minimum, maximum }`, with `0` and `Infinity` for missing bounds.

### getDefaultCoordinates

```ts
function getDefaultCoordinates(
	state: CropperState,
	settings: CoreSettings & InitializeSettings
): CoordinatesTransform | CoordinatesTransform[];
```

### getDefaultVisibleArea

```ts
function getDefaultVisibleArea(
	state: CropperState,
	settings: CoreSettings & InitializeSettings
): VisibleArea;
```

### getCoefficient

```ts
function getCoefficient(state: CropperState): number;
```

How many image pixels one screen pixel covers: `visibleArea.width / boundary.width`.

### getStencilCoordinates

```ts
function getStencilCoordinates(state: CropperState | null): Coordinates;
```

The crop in boundary pixels, which is where the stencil is drawn. All zeros when the state isn't initialized.

### getTransformedImageSize

```ts
function getTransformedImageSize(state: CropperState): Size;
```

The bounding size of the rotated image. Restrictions are expressed in this frame.

### getMinimumSize

```ts
function getMinimumSize(state: CropperState): number;
```

The smallest size, in image pixels, that a resize may produce: about 20 screen pixels, so the handles stay usable.

### isConsistentState

```ts
function isConsistentState(state: CropperState, settings: CoreSettings): boolean;
```

Whether the state already satisfies the settings, which means `reconcileState` would leave it unchanged.

## Image

### loadImage

```ts
function loadImage(
	src: string,
	settings?: { crossOrigin?: string | boolean; checkOrientation?: boolean; parse?: boolean }
): Promise<CropperImage>;
```

Loads an image and resolves with a [`CropperImage`](/docs/concept/introduction#image). With `checkOrientation`, it reads the JPEG's EXIF orientation, returns it as `transforms`, and serves a copy of the image with the orientation tag cleared. `crossOrigin` is set on the image element (`true` means `'anonymous'`). The promise rejects if the image fails to load. [`useCropperImage`](/docs/hooks/useCropperImage) wraps it with loading state.

### getBackgroundStyle

```ts
function getBackgroundStyle(
	image: CropperImage,
	state: CropperState,
	transitions?: CropperTransitions | null
): Record<string, string>;
```

The inline style that positions the image inside the boundary for the current visible area, including the CSS transition when `transitions.active` is set. `CropperBackgroundImage` uses it.

### getPreviewStyle

```ts
function getPreviewStyle(
	image: CropperImage,
	state: CropperState,
	size: Size,
	transitions?: CropperTransitions | null
): Record<string, string>;
```

The same for a preview of `size` that shows only the crop. `CropperPreview` uses it.

### getImageStyle

```ts
function getImageStyle(
	image: CropperImage,
	state: CropperState,
	area: Coordinates,
	coefficient: number,
	transitions?: CropperTransitions | null
): Record<string, string>;
```

The general form of the two above: the style that shows `area` of the image at the given scale.

These styles are objects with camelCase keys (`willChange`), as React expects. In Svelte, convert them to a style string before using them.

### getMimeType

```ts
import { getMimeType } from 'advanced-cropper/extensions/mimes';
```

```ts
function getMimeType(
	data: ArrayBuffer | string | null | undefined,
	fallback?: string | null
): string | undefined;
```

Detects an image's MIME type from its first bytes, for example from `CropperImage.arrayBuffer`. This one lives in a separate core entry point and is not re-exported, so install `advanced-cropper` as a direct dependency to import it.

## Size

### approximateSize

```ts
function approximateSize(params: {
	width: number;
	height: number;
	sizeRestrictions?: SizeRestrictions;
	aspectRatio?: RawAspectRatio;
}): Size;
```

Finds the size closest to `width` × `height` that satisfies both the size restrictions and the aspect ratio.

## State

### isEqualState

```ts
function isEqualState(a: CropperState | null, b: CropperState | null): boolean;
```

Compares two states deeply, treating numbers that differ by less than 0.001 as equal. See the [FAQ](/docs/faq#how-to-check-if-the-cropper-is-dirty) for an example.

### copyState

```ts
function copyState<T extends CropperState | null>(state: T): T;
```

A deep copy.

## Restrictions

### getBrokenRatio

```ts
function getBrokenRatio(currentAspectRatio: number, aspectRatio: AspectRatio): number | undefined;
```

If `currentAspectRatio` is outside the allowed range, returns the bound it broke. Otherwise returns `undefined`.

### fitToSizeRestrictions

```ts
function fitToSizeRestrictions(size: Size, sizeRestrictions: SizeRestrictions): number;
```

The scale factor that brings `size` within the restrictions while keeping its ratio (`1` if it already fits).

### resizeToSizeRestrictions

```ts
function resizeToSizeRestrictions(
	coordinates: Coordinates,
	sizeRestrictions: SizeRestrictions
): Coordinates;
```

Applies that scale factor.

### mergeSizeRestrictions

```ts
function mergeSizeRestrictions(a: SizeRestrictions, b: Partial<SizeRestrictions>): SizeRestrictions;
```

The intersection of two size restrictions.

### positionToSizeRestrictions

```ts
function positionToSizeRestrictions(positionRestrictions: PositionRestrictions): SizeRestrictions;
```

The largest size that fits between the position restrictions.

### mergePositionRestrictions

```ts
function mergePositionRestrictions(
	a: PositionRestrictions,
	b: PositionRestrictions
): PositionRestrictions;
```

The intersection of two position restrictions: the tighter value for each side.

### fitToPositionRestrictions

```ts
function fitToPositionRestrictions(
	coordinates: Coordinates,
	positionRestrictions: PositionRestrictions
): MoveDirections;
```

The move that brings the coordinates inside the restrictions.

### moveToPositionRestrictions

```ts
function moveToPositionRestrictions(
	coordinates: Coordinates,
	positionRestrictions: PositionRestrictions
): Coordinates;
```

Applies that move.

### coordinatesToPositionRestrictions

```ts
function coordinatesToPositionRestrictions(coordinates: Coordinates): PositionRestrictions;
```

Position restrictions that keep something inside the given rectangle.

## Geometry

### rotateSize

```ts
function rotateSize(size: Size, angle: number): Size;
```

The bounding size of `size` rotated by `angle` degrees.

### rotatePoint

```ts
function rotatePoint(point: Point, angle: number, anchor?: Point): Point;
```

Rotates a point by `angle` degrees around `anchor`, or around the origin.

### diff

```ts
function diff(firstObject: Point, secondObject: Point): Diff;
```

`firstObject - secondObject`, per axis.

### sizeDistance

```ts
function sizeDistance(a: Size, b: Size): number;
```

How different two sizes are, used to choose the closest candidate.

### getCenter

```ts
function getCenter(object: Coordinates): Point;
```

### getIntersections

```ts
function getIntersections(
	object: Coordinates,
	positionRestrictions: PositionRestrictions
): Intersections;
```

How far each side of `object` crosses the restrictions (`0` when it doesn't).

### applyDirections

```ts
function applyDirections(coordinates: Coordinates, directions: ResizeDirections): Coordinates;
```

Moves each side outward by the matching direction.

### applyMove

```ts
function applyMove(object: Coordinates, move: MoveDirections): Coordinates;
```

### inverseMove

```ts
function inverseMove(directions: MoveDirections): MoveDirections;
```

### applyScale

```ts
function applyScale(
	object: Coordinates,
	factor: number,
	center?: Point,
	progress?: number
): Coordinates;
```

Scales a rectangle by `factor` around `center` (its own centre by default).

### ratio

```ts
function ratio(object: Size): number;
```

`width / height`.

### maxScale

```ts
function maxScale(size: Size, restrictions: SizeRestrictions): number;
```

The largest factor `size` can be scaled by without breaking the maximums.

### minScale

```ts
function minScale(size: Size, restrictions: SizeRestrictions): number;
```

The smallest factor `size` can be scaled by without breaking the minimums.

## Math

### isRoughlyEqual

```ts
function isRoughlyEqual(a: number, b: number, tolerance?: number): boolean;
```

`true` when the numbers differ by less than `tolerance` (default `1e-3`).

### isGreater

```ts
function isGreater(a: number, b: number, tolerance?: number): boolean;
```

`a > b`, ignoring differences within the tolerance.

### isLower

```ts
function isLower(a: number, b: number, tolerance?: number): boolean;
```

`a < b`, ignoring differences within the tolerance.

### getCloserAngle

```ts
function getCloserAngle(reference: number, angle: number): number;
```

The angle equivalent to `angle` (plus or minus whole turns) that is closest to `reference`. See the [FAQ](/docs/faq#how-to-get-the-default-state) for why this is useful.
